# Content Creation workspace — API keys and secrets.
# Copy to `.env` (same folder) and fill in. `.env` is git-ignored and is
# auto-loaded by the media-use audio engine for any project up to 5 levels deep,
# and read by `studio doctor`.

# ElevenLabs — house primary TTS provider.
# Two conditions before it can produce a voiceover:
#   1. a paid plan (Creator or ≥$5 credits). Free-tier keys reject library
#      voices with HTTP 402 `paid_plan_required`.
#   2. a voice id, pasted into `.agents/design.md` → voice.voice_id. The engine
#      otherwise uses a hardcoded library voice your key cannot reach.
# Get a key at https://elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# Gemini TTS — the only proven Arabic (Egyptian) voice on this machine
# (voice `Kore`, lang `ar`). It is NOT in the engine's auto provider cascade,
# so it must be pinned: `studio voice <dir>` does that from BRIEF.md/design.md.
# Free tier ≈3 requests/minute — a 10-line narration needs pacing.
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# HeyGen — optional. When the host already sets HEYGEN_API_BASE, do not ask the
# user to sign in or offer OAuth. Only on explicit request otherwise.
# HEYGEN_API_KEY=
# HEYGEN_API_BASE=
